{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "synthesis:discussion/v1",
  "catalogId": "synthesis:discussion/v1",
  "protocolVersion": "1.0",
  "title": "Synthesis discussion catalog",
  "instructions": "Load the `a2ui` skill with `load_skill` before you compose a panel: it has the rules and examples. The essentials: `components` is a flat list; each component has a unique `id` and a `component` type, and exactly one has the id `root`. A container names its children by id. Bind a value with {\"@path\": \"/pointer\"} and give start values in `data_model`. For a common case use one card as `root`: ChoiceCard for a question with options, ConfirmCard for a yes or no decision, ComparisonCard for options against criteria, ChecklistCard for a set of items to keep. Example: [{\"id\":\"root\",\"component\":\"ConfirmCard\",\"title\":\"Apply the migration?\",\"confirm\":{\"label\":\"Apply\",\"name\":\"apply\"},\"decline\":{\"label\":\"Not now\",\"name\":\"skip\"}}]",
